1
00:00:12,200 --> 00:00:15,500
One hundred years have passed
since the Battle of Galluah Plains,

2
00:00:15,500 --> 00:00:18,910
where King Kyle defeated
the Dark Lord Angmund.

3
00:00:18,910 --> 00:00:22,450
The Demons rise again,
threatening the world,

4
00:00:22,450 --> 00:00:25,370
spreading fear and unrest to all.

5
00:00:25,370 --> 00:00:29,700
Kasel, an apprentice knight,
embarked on a journey to the King's Forest,

6
00:00:29,700 --> 00:00:34,750
to protect his friends,
those who are dearest to him.

7
00:00:34,750 --> 00:00:36,950
That's why I have to go.

8
00:00:36,950 --> 00:00:39,410
Go...? Go where?

9
00:00:40,580 --> 00:00:42,330
To find Clause.

10
00:02:12,870 --> 00:02:17,870
"The Truth, Revealed"

11
00:02:26,750 --> 00:02:27,790
Is that...?

12
00:02:42,080 --> 00:02:43,500
No...

13
00:02:50,700 --> 00:02:52,040
Mr. Flegg...

14
00:03:13,000 --> 00:03:14,290
Clause!

15
00:03:21,580 --> 00:03:23,410
This is Clause's shield...!

16
00:03:24,660 --> 00:03:25,950
No...

17
00:03:42,750 --> 00:03:45,000
It's... not Clause.

18
00:03:47,870 --> 00:03:49,200
Where are you going?

19
00:03:50,120 --> 00:03:51,450
I have to find Clause!

20
00:03:51,450 --> 00:03:52,950
Wait, Kasel!

21
00:03:55,870 --> 00:03:56,950
Frey!

22
00:04:05,700 --> 00:04:06,910
Demons...!

23
00:04:13,790 --> 00:04:15,000
Run, Frey!

24
00:04:15,000 --> 00:04:16,120
Kasel!

25
00:04:31,450 --> 00:04:33,500
Bring it on!

26
00:04:45,040 --> 00:04:46,080
Hurry!

27
00:04:51,330 --> 00:04:54,500
Let's play, boy.

28
00:05:00,000 --> 00:05:01,790
Kasel!

29
00:05:01,790 --> 00:05:05,660
Is that all? But still...

30
00:05:05,660 --> 00:05:07,250
He does have a resemblance...

31
00:05:17,040 --> 00:05:18,080
Frey!

32
00:05:26,450 --> 00:05:28,910
Riheet, we'll take care of these ones.

33
00:05:28,910 --> 00:05:30,250
Yeah.

34
00:05:31,250 --> 00:05:36,330
Just when I was having fun,
someone has to interfere.

35
00:06:05,330 --> 00:06:06,620
Incredible...

36
00:06:12,370 --> 00:06:13,790
Not bad.

37
00:06:16,580 --> 00:06:17,950
--This way!
--Yeah!

38
00:06:19,370 --> 00:06:22,250
Let's play again, boy.

39
00:06:32,200 --> 00:06:34,120
She got away...

40
00:06:34,120 --> 00:06:36,370
Who was that woman?

41
00:06:36,370 --> 00:06:37,370
A Demon, most likely.

42
00:06:37,370 --> 00:06:39,580
Looks like you're finished with the Demons.

43
00:06:40,290 --> 00:06:44,000
Aww, I wanted to get some action, too.

44
00:06:44,000 --> 00:06:46,120
Why didn't you leave some for me?

45
00:06:46,120 --> 00:06:47,700
You took too long to come.

46
00:06:49,660 --> 00:06:52,370
Brother, who are they?

47
00:06:52,370 --> 00:06:56,700
I am Kasel, a Guardian Knight of Orvelia.

48
00:06:56,700 --> 00:06:58,200
This is Frey.

49
00:06:59,870 --> 00:07:02,580
Thank you very much for saving us.

50
00:07:02,580 --> 00:07:07,160
We didn't save you. We were on
a mission to put down the Demons.

51
00:07:07,160 --> 00:07:09,000
A mission...?

52
00:07:09,000 --> 00:07:11,790
We are mercenaries, hired by Orvelia.

53
00:07:11,790 --> 00:07:13,540
By Orvelia?

54
00:07:13,540 --> 00:07:16,160
What are you two doing out here?

55
00:07:16,160 --> 00:07:19,040
You don't appear to be part
of the scouting party.

56
00:07:19,040 --> 00:07:22,790
We came out to see if our friend was safe.

57
00:07:22,790 --> 00:07:24,120
Huh?

58
00:07:25,290 --> 00:07:31,250
The scouts all died.
That's why we got dragged into this.

59
00:07:31,250 --> 00:07:34,450
I don't believe they all died...

60
00:07:34,450 --> 00:07:37,450
There must be survivors.

61
00:07:37,450 --> 00:07:39,500
Even after seeing this?

62
00:07:50,040 --> 00:07:51,290
Let's go.

63
00:07:51,290 --> 00:07:52,330
Yeah.

64
00:07:57,410 --> 00:07:58,580
Kasel.

65
00:08:03,330 --> 00:08:07,790
A healing spell. I can patch up small wounds.

66
00:08:07,790 --> 00:08:10,250
Thanks.

67
00:08:10,250 --> 00:08:16,500
I came to help Clause, but I couldn't even
defeat a single Demon by myself.

68
00:08:16,500 --> 00:08:19,410
How can I ever protect anyone like this...?

69
00:08:22,370 --> 00:08:24,080
Who is it?!

70
00:08:24,080 --> 00:08:27,000
Whoa, we're not the enemy.

71
00:08:27,000 --> 00:08:29,450
Don't be alarmed.

72
00:08:29,450 --> 00:08:31,950
Although I can't blame you,
given how suspicious this guy looks.

73
00:08:31,950 --> 00:08:33,080
Hey...

74
00:08:34,160 --> 00:08:37,120
For starters, can you put
the pointy object away?

75
00:08:40,700 --> 00:08:44,540
Thanks. I'm Cleo.

76
00:08:44,540 --> 00:08:45,910
I'm a sorceress!

77
00:08:48,750 --> 00:08:50,910
Sorceress...

78
00:08:50,910 --> 00:08:54,330
I'm Roi, her babysitter.

79
00:08:54,330 --> 00:08:56,160
You mean bodyguard.

80
00:08:56,160 --> 00:08:57,750
Basically the same.

81
00:08:57,750 --> 00:08:59,250
It's completely different!

82
00:08:59,250 --> 00:09:01,660
Um, so you two are...

83
00:09:03,040 --> 00:09:07,950
We've come looking for you.
You're Kasel and Frey, right?

84
00:09:07,950 --> 00:09:09,660
How did you know...?

85
00:09:09,660 --> 00:09:12,410
Oh, great! We didn't get the wrong people!

86
00:09:12,410 --> 00:09:16,000
I want to take you somewhere. Follow me!

87
00:09:16,000 --> 00:09:17,500
What do you mean?

88
00:09:17,500 --> 00:09:19,500
You'll know if you follow me.

89
00:09:20,910 --> 00:09:22,080
Let's go.

90
00:09:31,830 --> 00:09:33,250
We're here!

91
00:09:33,250 --> 00:09:37,620
Here? There doesn't seem to be anything here.

92
00:09:37,620 --> 00:09:39,370
What's this about?

93
00:09:39,370 --> 00:09:43,330
Come on, calm down. I'll explain.

94
00:09:43,330 --> 00:09:45,410
A certain person asked for our help.

95
00:09:45,410 --> 00:09:47,910
He told us that you two are
headed for the King's Forest,

96
00:09:47,910 --> 00:09:49,910
and he wanted us to bring you here.

97
00:09:49,910 --> 00:09:51,950
A certain person...?

98
00:09:51,950 --> 00:09:53,370
It's Dominix.

99
00:09:54,450 --> 00:09:55,700
Dominix?!

100
00:09:55,700 --> 00:09:58,290
You mean the sorcerer
who's in the Tower of the Sage?

101
00:09:58,290 --> 00:10:01,910
Yes. I've been told you know each other.

102
00:10:01,910 --> 00:10:06,660
Yes, he visited us at the orphanage
where we grew up.

103
00:10:06,660 --> 00:10:08,790
But why him...?

104
00:10:08,790 --> 00:10:11,580
Dominix will fill you in on the details.

105
00:10:11,580 --> 00:10:13,910
All right, let's get going already.

106
00:10:13,910 --> 00:10:16,250
Go...? Go where?

107
00:10:16,250 --> 00:10:17,830
Isn't it obvious?

108
00:10:18,750 --> 00:10:20,040
Up!

109
00:10:37,910 --> 00:10:39,250
Up?

110
00:10:39,250 --> 00:10:41,830
That's right, the Tower of the Sage.

111
00:10:41,830 --> 00:10:47,330
But how? And I thought only the chosen
get to enter the Tower of the Sage...

112
00:10:49,370 --> 00:10:51,910
You're looking at a chosen one.

113
00:10:51,910 --> 00:10:53,330
Me!

114
00:10:57,500 --> 00:10:59,200
And now...

115
00:10:59,200 --> 00:11:01,040
Going up!

116
00:11:23,620 --> 00:11:25,620
We're here!

117
00:11:28,410 --> 00:11:30,120
Incredible...!

118
00:11:36,540 --> 00:11:38,500
Hey, you two!

119
00:11:38,500 --> 00:11:41,160
What are you doing? Get over here.

120
00:11:48,000 --> 00:11:53,950
Most of the people here are sorcerers
or scholars training under the Great Sage.

121
00:11:53,950 --> 00:11:57,540
The Great Sage... What is he like?

122
00:11:57,540 --> 00:11:59,830
What he's like...

123
00:11:59,830 --> 00:12:04,120
In one word: freak.
He's supposed to be super old,

124
00:12:04,120 --> 00:12:07,000
but he maintains his youth
using his magical powers.

125
00:12:07,000 --> 00:12:11,160
Choose your words wisely.
What if someone hears you?

126
00:12:11,160 --> 00:12:14,540
I don't care, it's the truth.

127
00:12:25,290 --> 00:12:26,620
I brought them.

128
00:12:31,450 --> 00:12:33,040
Mr. Dominix!

129
00:12:33,040 --> 00:12:36,750
I've been waiting for you, Kasel, Frey.

130
00:12:36,750 --> 00:12:38,370
It's been a long time.

131
00:12:38,370 --> 00:12:42,540
I think the last time we saw you
was when we left the orphanage.

132
00:12:42,540 --> 00:12:46,750
Yes. I see the two of you
are all grown up now.

133
00:12:46,750 --> 00:12:49,540
You haven't changed at all, Mr. Dominix.

134
00:12:49,540 --> 00:12:54,080
Yes, really... You look exactly like
the last time we saw you.

135
00:12:54,080 --> 00:12:56,830
Like I said, he's a freak.

136
00:12:57,540 --> 00:12:59,750
He's the Great Sage.

137
00:13:00,910 --> 00:13:05,450
We thought you were just a sorcerer
who came to visit us at the orphanage...

138
00:13:06,830 --> 00:13:10,910
Revealing my identity tends
to cause unwanted trouble.

139
00:13:10,910 --> 00:13:13,120
I see...

140
00:13:13,120 --> 00:13:16,250
Great Sage, why did you bring us here?

141
00:13:16,250 --> 00:13:18,370
Just call me Dominix.

142
00:13:18,370 --> 00:13:20,950
There's someone I want you to see.

143
00:13:35,580 --> 00:13:36,870
Clause!

144
00:13:37,700 --> 00:13:41,700
He's quite heavily injured, but not fatally.

145
00:13:41,700 --> 00:13:44,790
Give him a while, and he'll be back on his feet.

146
00:13:44,790 --> 00:13:46,290
I'm so relieved...

147
00:13:46,290 --> 00:13:48,330
Yes, really...

148
00:13:48,330 --> 00:13:52,950
We detected Demonic activities,
so Cleo and I went to help them.

149
00:13:52,950 --> 00:13:54,290
But...

150
00:13:54,290 --> 00:13:56,660
He was the only survivor.

151
00:13:58,250 --> 00:14:02,450
Mr. Dominix, did you know we were coming?

152
00:14:02,450 --> 00:14:05,200
Yes, I was watching from here.

153
00:14:07,580 --> 00:14:08,660
Clause!

154
00:14:11,620 --> 00:14:14,790
Kasel...? Frey...?

155
00:14:19,580 --> 00:14:24,080
I see... So Gran did make it back to the castle.

156
00:14:24,080 --> 00:14:26,950
We were so worried about you, Clause...

157
00:14:26,950 --> 00:14:28,750
So you came out here, all by yourselves?

158
00:14:28,750 --> 00:14:30,000
Yeah.

159
00:14:30,000 --> 00:14:32,830
So reckless...

160
00:14:34,410 --> 00:14:38,910
The Demons came out of nowhere
and surrounded us.

161
00:14:38,910 --> 00:14:40,790
We couldn't even escape.

162
00:14:42,080 --> 00:14:47,040
A band of mercenaries sent
from Orvelia took out the Demons.

163
00:14:47,040 --> 00:14:49,540
That female Demon ran off, too.

164
00:14:49,540 --> 00:14:51,500
Female Demon?

165
00:14:51,500 --> 00:14:54,160
In other words, a witch, right?

166
00:14:54,160 --> 00:14:56,120
So you didn't see her, Clause?

167
00:14:56,120 --> 00:15:00,750
No. All we fought were
the skeleton-looking Demons.

168
00:15:00,750 --> 00:15:04,080
So... That witch...

169
00:15:04,080 --> 00:15:07,700
She's not related to the Demons
that attacked the scouts?

170
00:15:07,700 --> 00:15:11,330
We don't know. Who could she be...?

171
00:15:13,750 --> 00:15:17,120
Now, let's let Clause rest.

172
00:15:17,120 --> 00:15:20,120
You two should stay here for a while.

173
00:15:20,120 --> 00:15:21,120
Thank you.

174
00:15:21,120 --> 00:15:24,000
Thank you, Mr. Dominix.

175
00:15:24,000 --> 00:15:27,580
Cleo, Roi, please take care of them.

176
00:15:27,580 --> 00:15:29,120
Oh, sure.

177
00:15:32,580 --> 00:15:36,950
You can use this room.
Let me know if you need anything.

178
00:15:36,950 --> 00:15:38,580
Thank you.

179
00:15:38,580 --> 00:15:40,450
Don't worry about it.

180
00:15:40,450 --> 00:15:44,700
By the way, are you sure you didn't
want to be in a room with Kasel?

181
00:15:44,700 --> 00:15:47,870
K-Kasel and I aren't like that!

182
00:15:47,870 --> 00:15:52,790
Oh, really? You two looked
good for each other.

183
00:15:52,790 --> 00:15:55,290
Please don't tease.

184
00:15:55,290 --> 00:15:57,120
Sorry!

185
00:15:57,120 --> 00:16:00,500
We're really alike. We should be friends!

186
00:16:00,500 --> 00:16:01,500
Huh?

187
00:16:01,500 --> 00:16:04,500
You said you were at an orphanage, right?

188
00:16:04,500 --> 00:16:07,910
I don't have parents, either.
Dominix found me.

189
00:16:07,910 --> 00:16:09,540
I see...

190
00:16:11,500 --> 00:16:14,790
I do enjoy life here at the Tower of the Sage.

191
00:16:14,790 --> 00:16:21,160
I learn all sorts of things all the time,
and train as a sorceress, too.

192
00:16:21,160 --> 00:16:23,330
But...

193
00:16:23,330 --> 00:16:25,120
It can get a bit boring!

194
00:16:34,700 --> 00:16:36,410
The stars are so pretty.

195
00:16:36,410 --> 00:16:40,790
This place is boring,
but the night sky is the best.

196
00:16:46,200 --> 00:16:47,410
Is that...?

197
00:16:48,330 --> 00:16:53,290
I'll be off then. Let me know
if you need anything.

198
00:16:53,290 --> 00:16:54,620
Thank you.

199
00:17:09,080 --> 00:17:10,290
Kasel.

200
00:17:11,620 --> 00:17:13,660
What are you doing here?

201
00:17:14,370 --> 00:17:15,540
Frey...

202
00:17:19,200 --> 00:17:22,370
If I had strength...

203
00:17:25,160 --> 00:17:30,250
...I could have fought those Demons together
with Clause and the others!

204
00:17:31,250 --> 00:17:35,450
When the Demons attacked
the village back then...

205
00:17:35,450 --> 00:17:37,620
...my mother died protecting me.

206
00:17:39,500 --> 00:17:43,620
I don't ever want to lose
someone precious to me.

207
00:17:43,620 --> 00:17:47,120
I want to be able to protect them!

208
00:17:47,120 --> 00:17:49,330
But...

209
00:17:49,330 --> 00:17:50,540
Kasel...

210
00:17:54,080 --> 00:17:56,620
I can't go on like this.

211
00:17:56,620 --> 00:17:58,830
I have to become stronger.

212
00:18:02,250 --> 00:18:05,450
The Black Edge have returned.

213
00:18:05,450 --> 00:18:07,790
We took out the Demons.

214
00:18:07,790 --> 00:18:09,040
Here's the proof.

215
00:18:11,160 --> 00:18:12,790
Oh, how inauspicious!

216
00:18:12,790 --> 00:18:14,910
Don't bring such a thing into the castle!

217
00:18:14,910 --> 00:18:17,370
P-Put that away, now!

218
00:18:17,370 --> 00:18:21,750
Now you must see what
the Black Edge are capable of.

219
00:18:21,750 --> 00:18:25,750
With their service, Demons are not to fear.

220
00:18:25,750 --> 00:18:27,410
But they are...

221
00:18:27,410 --> 00:18:31,330
So they are dark elves, what is the issue?

222
00:18:33,080 --> 00:18:37,080
To destroy the Demons,
all races must work together.

223
00:18:37,080 --> 00:18:41,950
Just like King Kyle, who worked
with allies like the elves and orcs

224
00:18:41,950 --> 00:18:44,000
to defeat the Dark Lord 100 years ago.

225
00:18:46,120 --> 00:18:48,870
We thank you for your efforts.

226
00:18:48,870 --> 00:18:53,450
Get rid of that Demon head.
It must not be seen by the populace.

227
00:18:54,500 --> 00:18:55,660
I understand.

228
00:19:02,120 --> 00:19:04,620
Did you see the looks on their faces?

229
00:19:04,620 --> 00:19:09,250
Just showing them the Demon head
almost made them collapse in fear.

230
00:19:12,540 --> 00:19:16,790
Orvelia is lead by cowards like them.

231
00:19:16,790 --> 00:19:22,120
Behl, the Chancellor, might be diligent,
but he is incapable of any action!

232
00:19:23,250 --> 00:19:28,290
I, El Moriham, descend from
a long line of Orvelian Chancellors.

233
00:19:28,290 --> 00:19:33,290
Me ascending to the rank of
Chancellor is a family wish as well.

234
00:19:33,290 --> 00:19:36,790
We will silence those fools
and make them do our bidding,

235
00:19:36,790 --> 00:19:40,040
but for that to happen,
you must deliver results.

236
00:19:40,040 --> 00:19:42,660
Yes, I understand.

237
00:19:42,660 --> 00:19:46,500
It was truly fortuitous that
you and I met, Riheet...

238
00:19:46,500 --> 00:19:51,000
If my wish comes true,
you all will live a good life.

239
00:19:51,000 --> 00:19:54,790
It wouldn't be out of the question
for you to become a noble.

240
00:19:57,080 --> 00:19:58,830
To our future.

241
00:20:05,580 --> 00:20:07,700
Clause, how are you doing?

242
00:20:07,700 --> 00:20:09,450
I'm fine.

243
00:20:09,450 --> 00:20:11,830
We have to go back to Orvelia
as soon as possible.

244
00:20:13,040 --> 00:20:14,700
Don't push yourself too hard.

245
00:20:14,700 --> 00:20:18,000
Maybe you should rest a bit more.

246
00:20:18,000 --> 00:20:21,040
Who knows when the Demons might strike again?

247
00:20:21,040 --> 00:20:22,540
I can't relax now.

248
00:20:22,540 --> 00:20:23,790
But...

249
00:20:24,830 --> 00:20:28,750
I survived so that I can defeat the Demons.

250
00:20:28,750 --> 00:20:34,080
For the friends who've died,
I will use my life for Orvelia.

251
00:20:34,080 --> 00:20:35,950
Clause...

252
00:20:35,950 --> 00:20:37,750
Kasel, Frey.

253
00:20:38,700 --> 00:20:42,950
Dominix wants to see you.
He says it's important.

254
00:20:48,620 --> 00:20:50,870
They're here.

255
00:20:50,870 --> 00:20:54,790
Thank you. You're dismissed, Cleo.

256
00:20:54,790 --> 00:20:56,950
Sure.

257
00:20:56,950 --> 00:21:01,500
So what's the important issue?

258
00:21:01,500 --> 00:21:04,040
There is something I need to tell you.

259
00:21:05,080 --> 00:21:08,080
Frey, you should hear this, too.

260
00:21:08,080 --> 00:21:09,450
Yes...

261
00:21:12,660 --> 00:21:14,830
--Hey.
--Shh!

262
00:21:14,830 --> 00:21:19,750
Your mother--Arlette--had she
ever told you about your father?

263
00:21:19,750 --> 00:21:20,750
No.

264
00:21:20,750 --> 00:21:27,120
I asked her not to tell you
anything until the right time.

265
00:21:27,120 --> 00:21:28,750
What do you mean?

266
00:21:30,410 --> 00:21:36,700
You are the son of King Kyle,
who fought Dark Lord Angmund 100 years ago.

267
